author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Add an isolated real-Git shared-prefix add/add regression distinct from independent identity collisions; Preserve both streams through authenticated settlement or recoverable actionable refusal; Keep the existing ambiguous-creation refusal and history-hash invariants; Make conflict status and health/reconciliation guidance explicit for operator resolution
definition_of_ready: "Report, open settlement lineage and completed ancestry guard were read; require an isolated real-Git reproduction and explicit preservation policy before implementation"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Keep multi-agent context lossless or explicitly recoverable at empty-Git-base merge boundaries
value: Agents can resolve structured conflicts without treating marker-free content as a proven lossless merge
why_now: A fresh published-version report identifies a potentially destructive operator-resolution boundary not covered by the current read-context delivery
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: 75
resolution: "The Git driver preserves both full source snapshots inside explicit conflict markers when creation ancestry is ambiguous, retaining existing identity authentication. Real-Git tests exercise both newline checkout policies without weakening record or hash comparisons."
expected_result: "Ambiguous add/add identity refuses automatic fusion while retaining both complete branch snapshots in visible conflict artifacts, and staged unresolved markers remain unhealthy on every supported checkout policy."
actual_result: "The final shared58-test linked journey passed, including the8-case LF/CRLF real-Git matrix. Original-main negative controls fail at the intended marker-preservation boundary. Final native Windows and macOS hosted checks remain mandatory before merge."
