comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T12:32:22.626Z","harness:codex","Live duplicate check: keyword add/add search returned eight historical items; full metadata/history reads of the completed identity guard and history-driver foundation plus open settlement UX establish distinct boundaries. The closed identity fix intentionally rejects empty-ancestor identical creates and remains completed. This new report covers shared-prefix add/add conflict artifacts and safe operator resolution; keep it open and unclaimed for isolated reproduction, with no implementation claimed in PR 1490."
  "2026-10-18T13:57:24.913Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: reproduce the shared-prefix cherry-pick add/add boundary in an isolated real Git repository. Retain the completed pm-qx95lz ancestry guard: copied create bytes are not independent identity authentication. On refusal, preserve both input snapshots visibly so staging a marker-free preferred side cannot appear lossless. Group with pm-gh1475 settlement safety."
  "2026-10-18T14:11:14.740Z","harness:codex","Isolated real-Git reproduction uses distinct planning-commit identities after cherry-pick so the merge base truly lacks the item. Both item and history drivers retain the completed identity-ancestry refusal, preserve both exact source snapshots within visible conflict markers, and keep health failing after the conflicted files are staged. Pure merge semantics still reject identical independent creates."
  "2026-10-18T16:52:17.786Z","harness:codex","Verification: the complete suite passed10690 tests with3 platform skips. Its exact coverage report identified only the driver passthrough and tracker-at-Git-root hook cases; both are now covered by real filesystem tests, and the231-test focused run reports exact100/100/100/100 for driver.ts and install.ts. The two new helper modules also passed exact100/100/100/100. All linked PM tests were rerun successfully. The complete static pipeline, all TypeScript projects, release-version policy, tracked-secret scan, registry inventory and sequential npm/npx/Bun packed smoke passed. Final hosted full-population coverage and native-platform checks remain mandatory before merge; this closure records implemented, locally verified work for the reviewed delivery, not a new registry publication."
  "2026-10-18T17:59:57.088Z","harness:codex","Windows CI and CodeRabbit identified LF/CRLF assumptions in the snapshot assertions. Tests now run both checkout policies on every host, normalize only line endings for complete-text comparisons, retain every JSON record/hash, and verify the clone actually uses the requested newline policy. The existing ancestry guard remains intentional: copied create bytes alone do not authorize identity fusion, and the planned acceptance permits a recoverable visible refusal. All linked test sets passed the checkout correction before index-proof review hardening."
  "2026-10-18T18:44:11.521Z","harness:codex","Review verification: the shared58-test linked journey passed on the final revision. All8 real-Git scenarios run both LF and CRLF policies; complete-text assertions normalize only line endings, verify the clone checkout policy, and preserve full records and hashes. Both ambiguous add/add snapshots remain visible and staged markers keep health failing. The completed independent-creation ancestry guard remains intact; no copied-prefix identity fusion was introduced."
